.TH "XRWM" "1" "September 2026" "xrwm 0.1.1" "xrwm Manual"
.SH NAME
xrwm \- River 0.4+ dynamic tiling Wayland window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]xrwm\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]xrwm\f[R] \f[I]command\f[R] [\f[I]arguments\&...\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]xrwm\f[R] is an ultra\-lightweight, memory\-safe Wayland window
manager built for \f[B]river(1)\f[R] 0.4+, written in Rust.
.PP
It combines the architectural process separation of River 0.4 with the
beloved 32\-bit tag bitmask, dynamic master\-stack tiling, and
composable shell\-script configuration of river\-classic.
.PP
When run without arguments, \f[B]xrwm\f[R] acts as the window manager
daemon and connects to the running \f[B]river(1)\f[R] compositor.
When run with arguments, it acts as a client controller communicating
with the daemon over a UNIX domain socket.
.SH TERMINOLOGY
.TP
\f[I]view\f[R]
A managed application window (e.g.\ an xdg\-toplevel).
.TP
\f[I]output\f[R]
A logical screen or monitor display area.
.TP
\f[I]tag\f[R]
A 32\-bit bitmask identifying workspace assignment (from 1 to 32).
A view may belong to multiple tags, and multiple tags may be focused
simultaneously.
.TP
\f[I]master\f[R]
The primary column or row in the tiling layout.
.TP
\f[I]stack\f[R]
The secondary area of windows arranged beside the master area.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS WINDOW ACTIONS
.TP
\f[B]close\f[R]
Closes the currently focused window gracefully.
.TP
\f[B]zoom\f[R]
Promotes the focused window to the master position in the layout stack.
If the master window is already focused, promotes the second view in the
stack to master (toggles between the two most active windows).
.TP
\f[B]toggle\-float\f[R]
Toggles floating or tiled state on the focused window.
When returning to floating, preserves its previous floating geometry.
.TP
\f[B]toggle\-fullscreen\f[R]
Toggles fullscreen state on the focused window.
.TP
\f[B]focus\-view\f[R] [\f[B]\-skip\-floating\f[R]] \f[I]direction\f[R]
Shifts window focus in the specified direction.
Supported directions are \f[B]next\f[R], \f[B]previous\f[R] (or
\f[B]prev\f[R]), \f[B]left\f[R], \f[B]right\f[R], \f[B]up\f[R], and
\f[B]down\f[R].
If \f[B]\-skip\-floating\f[R] is passed, floating windows are ignored
during navigation.
.TP
\f[B]swap\f[R] \f[I]direction\f[R]
Swaps the focused window with the window in the specified direction
(\f[B]next\f[R], \f[B]previous\f[R], \f[B]left\f[R], \f[B]right\f[R],
\f[B]up\f[R], \f[B]down\f[R]).
Allows reordering within the secondary stack without disturbing the
master view.
.TP
\f[B]focus\-output\f[R] \f[I]direction\f[R]
Shifts focus across displays in the specified logical or spatial
direction (\f[B]next\f[R], \f[B]previous\f[R], \f[B]left\f[R],
\f[B]right\f[R], \f[B]up\f[R], \f[B]down\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]send\-to\-output\f[R] [\f[B]\-current\-tags\f[R]] \f[I]direction\f[R]
Sends the focused window to the target output in the specified
direction.
If \f[B]\-current\-tags\f[R] is passed, automatically updates the
window\(cqs tag mask to match the active tags of the destination output.
.TP
\f[B]resize\f[R] \f[B]horizontal\f[R]|\f[B]vertical\f[R] \f[I]delta\f[R]
Resizes floating windows by \f[I]delta\f[R] pixels, or adjusts tiled
layout proportions (\f[B]horizontal\f[R] adjusts \f[B]main\-ratio\f[R];
\f[B]vertical\f[R] adjusts \f[B]stack\-ratio\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]move\f[R] \f[B]left\f[R]|\f[B]right\f[R]|\f[B]up\f[R]|\f[B]down\f[R] \f[I]delta\f[R]
Translates a floating window by \f[I]delta\f[R] logical pixels.
Ignored on tiled windows.
.TP
\f[B]snap\f[R] \f[B]left\f[R]|\f[B]right\f[R]|\f[B]up\f[R]|\f[B]down\f[R]
Converts the focused window to floating and snaps it to cover the
corresponding half of the screen (50% width on left/right, or 50% height
on up/down).
.TP
\f[B]spawn\f[R] \f[I]command\f[R]
Spawns an external application process with arguments (typically used in
keybindings: \f[CR]map normal Super Return spawn foot\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]exit\f[R]
Terminates the \f[B]xrwm\f[R] window manager daemon.
.TP
\f[B]reload\f[R]
Re\-executes the user configuration script
(\f[CR]\(ti/.config/xrwm/init\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]ping\f[R]
Health check request, returning \f[CR]pong\f[R].
.SS TAG MANAGEMENT
.TP
\f[B]set\-focused\-tags\f[R] \f[I]tags\f[R]
Sets the visible tag bitmask on the current output.
.TP
\f[B]set\-view\-tags\f[R] \f[I]tags\f[R]
Sets the tag bitmask assignment of the currently focused window.
.TP
\f[B]toggle\-focused\-tags\f[R] \f[I]tags\f[R]
Toggles the visibility of the specified tag bits on the current output.
Enables viewing multiple tags simultaneously or toggling scratchpads
(tag 32).
.TP
\f[B]toggle\-view\-tags\f[R] \f[I]tags\f[R]
Toggles the specified tag bits on the currently focused window.
.TP
\f[B]focus\-previous\-tags\f[R]
Jumps back and forth between the current and previous tag configuration.
.TP
\f[B]send\-to\-previous\-tags\f[R]
Sends the focused window to the previous tag configuration.
.TP
\f[B]spawn\-tagmask\f[R] \f[I]tags\f[R]
Sets a bitmask restricting the initial tag assignment of newly created
views.
New windows receive \f[CR]focused_tags & spawn_tagmask\f[R].
Defaults to \f[CR]0xFFFFFFFF\f[R].
.SS LAYOUT CONFIGURATION
.TP
\f[B]view\-padding\f[R] \f[I]pixels\f[R]
Sets the inner padding between windows in pixels.
Defaults to \f[CR]4\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]outer\-padding\f[R] \f[I]pixels\f[R]
Sets the outer padding between the window layout perimeter and the
screen edge in pixels.
Defaults to \f[CR]4\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]main\-location\f[R] \f[B]left\f[R]|\f[B]right\f[R]|\f[B]top\f[R]|\f[B]bottom\f[R]
Sets the placement orientation of the master area.
Defaults to \f[B]left\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]main\-count\f[R] \f[I]count\f[R]
Sets the number of windows allocated to the master area.
Can be absolute (e.g.\ \f[CR]2\f[R]) or relative (e.g.\ \f[CR]+1\f[R],
\f[CR]\-1\f[R]).
Defaults to \f[CR]1\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]main\-ratio\f[R] \f[I]ratio\f[R]
Sets the master area proportion relative to the layout area, clamped to
\f[CR]0.1\f[R]..\f[CR]0.9\f[R].
Can be absolute (e.g.\ \f[CR]0.60\f[R]) or relative
(e.g.\ \f[CR]+0.05\f[R], \f[CR]\-0.05\f[R]).
Defaults to \f[CR]0.55\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]stack\-ratio\f[R] \f[I]ratio\f[R]
Sets the secondary stack height division proportion, clamped to
\f[CR]0.1\f[R]..\f[CR]0.9\f[R].
Can be absolute (e.g.\ \f[CR]0.65\f[R]) or relative
(e.g.\ \f[CR]+0.05\f[R], \f[CR]\-0.05\f[R]).
Defaults to \f[CR]0.50\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]default\-attach\-mode\f[R] \f[B]top\f[R]|\f[B]bottom\f[R]|\f[B]above\f[R]|\f[B]below\f[R]|\f[B]after\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]
Sets the insertion position for newly created windows in the stack:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]top\f[R]: Inserts at the top of the stack (becomes master).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]bottom\f[R]: Appends to the end of the stack.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]above\f[R]: Inserts above the currently focused window.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]below\f[R]: Inserts below the currently focused window.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]after\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]: Inserts after \f[I]N\f[R] windows in the
stack.
.SS APPEARANCE & POLICIES
.TP
\f[B]border\-width\f[R] \f[I]pixels\f[R]
Sets server\-side decoration (SSD) border thickness in pixels.
Defaults to \f[CR]2\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]border\-color\-focused\f[R] \f[I]color\f[R]
Sets the border color of the focused window (hex format
\f[CR]#RRGGBB\f[R] or \f[CR]0xRRGGBB\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]border\-color\-unfocused\f[R] \f[I]color\f[R]
Sets the border color of unfocused windows.
.TP
\f[B]border\-color\-urgent\f[R] \f[I]color\f[R]
Sets the border color of windows demanding urgency attention.
.TP
\f[B]set\-cursor\-warp\f[R] \f[B]disabled\f[R]|\f[B]on\-output\-change\f[R]|\f[B]on\-focus\-change\f[R]
Configures cursor warp policy:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]disabled\f[R]: Cursor is never automatically warped.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]on\-output\-change\f[R]: Cursor automatically warps to the center
of the destination screen on output focus change.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]on\-focus\-change\f[R]: Cursor warps to the center of the newly
focused window or screen.
.TP
\f[B]focus\-follows\-cursor\f[R] \f[B]disabled\f[R]|\f[B]normal\f[R]|\f[B]always\f[R]
Configures pointer hover focus policy:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]normal\f[R]: Automatically focuses views when the pointer crosses
over borders.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]disabled\f[R]: Pointer movement does not alter keyboard focus; only
clicks or key bindings change focus.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]always\f[R]: The view under the pointer is always focused on any
movement.
.TP
\f[B]hide\-cursor\f[R] \f[B]timeout\f[R] \f[I]milliseconds\f[R]
Automatically hides the cursor after \f[I]milliseconds\f[R] of
inactivity.
Set to \f[CR]0\f[R] to disable.
.TP
\f[B]hide\-cursor\f[R] \f[B]when\-typing\f[R] \f[B]enabled\f[R]|\f[B]disabled\f[R]
Automatically hides the cursor when typing on the keyboard.
Moving the pointer immediately restores visibility.
.TP
\f[B]animation\f[R] \f[B]true\f[R]|\f[B]false\f[R]
Enables or disables window geometry and workspace slide transition
animations.
Defaults to \f[CR]true\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]animation\-duration\f[R] \f[I]milliseconds\f[R]
Sets the cubic ease\-out animation transition duration in milliseconds.
Defaults to \f[CR]150\f[R].
.SS MAPPINGS & MODES
.TP
\f[B]declare\-mode\f[R] \f[I]mode\f[R]
Declares a new custom modal keybinding mode.
.TP
\f[B]enter\-mode\f[R] \f[I]mode\f[R]
Enters the specified keybinding mode (built\-in modes include
\f[B]normal\f[R] and \f[B]locked\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]map\f[R] \f[I]mode\f[R] \f[I]modifiers\f[R] \f[I]key\f[R] \f[I]action\&...\f[R]
Maps a keyboard key combination in \f[I]mode\f[R] to execute an action.
Modifiers include \f[CR]Super\f[R] (or \f[CR]Mod4\f[R]),
\f[CR]Shift\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl\f[R], \f[CR]Alt\f[R] (or \f[CR]Mod1\f[R]),
\f[CR]None\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]map\-pointer\f[R] \f[I]mode\f[R] \f[I]modifiers\f[R] \f[I]button\f[R] \f[I]action\&...\f[R]
Maps a mouse button press in \f[I]mode\f[R] to an action
(e.g.\ \f[CR]BTN_LEFT move\-view\f[R],
\f[CR]BTN_RIGHT resize\-view\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]unmap\f[R] \f[I]mode\f[R] \f[I]modifiers\f[R] \f[I]key\f[R]
Dynamically unregisters a key binding in \f[I]mode\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]unmap\-pointer\f[R] \f[I]mode\f[R] \f[I]modifiers\f[R] \f[I]button\f[R]
Dynamically unregisters a mouse pointer binding in \f[I]mode\f[R].
.SS WINDOW RULES
.TP
\f[B]rule\-add\f[R] [\f[B]\-app\-id\f[R] \f[I]glob\f[R]] [\f[B]\-title\f[R] \f[I]glob\f[R]] \f[I]action\f[R] [\f[I]arguments\&...\f[R]]
Adds a window matching rule.
\f[I]glob\f[R] supports standard wildcards (\f[CR]*\f[R]).
Available actions:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]float\f[R] / \f[B]no\-float\f[R]: Force floating or tiled mode.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]ssd\f[R] / \f[B]csd\f[R]: Force server\-side borders or
client\-side decorations.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]tags\f[R] \f[I]mask\f[R]: Assign initial tag bitmask.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]dimensions\f[R] \f[I]width\f[R] \f[I]height\f[R]: Set initial
floating width and height (centered).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]position\f[R] \f[I]x\f[R] \f[I]y\f[R]: Set initial floating window
position.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]fullscreen\f[R]: Automatically launch window in fullscreen mode.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]output\f[R] \f[I]name|id\f[R]: Assign initial target display.
.TP
\f[B]rule\-del\f[R] [\f[B]\-app\-id\f[R] \f[I]glob\f[R]] [\f[B]\-title\f[R] \f[I]glob\f[R]] \f[I]action\f[R]
Deletes a previously added window rule matching the criteria.
.TP
\f[B]list\-rules\f[R] [\f[I]action\f[R]]
Prints all active window rules, optionally filtered by action type.
.SS STATUS & QUERY
.TP
\f[B]status\f[R] [\f[B]\(enformat\f[R] \f[B]waybar\f[R]] [\f[B]\(enstream\f[R]]
Queries window manager state.
Without flags, outputs a single JSON object with tags, window list,
geometry, and layout details.
With \f[B]\(enformat waybar\f[R], outputs formatted JSON for Waybar
custom modules.
With \f[B]\(enstream\f[R], maintains a persistent pipe streaming JSON
updates on every state change.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xrwm/init\f[R] or \f[CR]\(ti/.config/xrwm/init\f[R]
User configuration script executed upon daemon startup and reloaded via
\f[CR]xrwm reload\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/xrwm\-$WAYLAND_DISPLAY.sock\f[R]
UNIX domain socket used for IPC communication.
If \f[CR]$WAYLAND_DISPLAY\f[R] contains path separators, special
characters, or exceeds safe length bounds, a sanitized prefix and stable
hash are used instead.
When \f[CR]$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\f[R] exceeds socket length limits, a
user\-private fallback directory under \f[CR]/tmp/xrwm\-<uid>/\f[R] is
used.
